A||N||10||Dan87GT||electric truck release problem||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||11-20-2000||08:25 AM||||Hello, my electric trunk release does not work. I was trying to trouble shoot it. And I    am confused about the wiring. The are 4 wires from the connector at the passenger side, 1 ground at the driver side. I believe it gets the ground connection from the latch on the trunk. Can anybody explain how this works? Why 4 wires into the trunk lid?||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-20-2000||09:05 AM||||Two of the wires are for the "Ajar" switch on the inst. panel.<P>Try energizing the solenoid on the trunk release with 12 volts direct. If this works, it pretty much eliminates the solenoid and you can concentrate on the relay or the switch/wiring. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan87GT||11-20-2000||09:22 AM||||Is there a switch inside the decklid? So for it to work the deck has to be closed, correct? and the ignition off?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-20-2000||09:50 AM||||The ajar switch is located on the frame next to the driver's side shock tower (on mine anyway).  It's only purpose is to control the ajar light on the dash.  The wire clipped to the metal sheet on the underside of the deck is just a ground.  As far as I know no switches are inside the deck.<P>The ignition needs to be in the On position for the electric trunk release to work.  The trunk solinoid should fire whether the deck is closed or open.||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||11-20-2000||11:40 AM||||84 and 85 trunk releases are different than the 86-88. The older ones have 2 wires that go just to the solenoid. My 86 trunk releases do not require the ignition to be on or the emergency brake to be set. They are both original factory installed. The switch on the release turns on the trunk light. Never saw the 'ajar' light come on when the trunk was open, key on or off. The lid will start to rise up as you increase speed and blocks your rear view if you forget to slam it down. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-20-2000||01:00 PM||||Remove the switch from the dash bezel and shake it. If it rattles then all you need is a new (or good used) switch.  <P>If it checks out then you may need a new relay....it's under the dash.<P>It sounds like it just suddenly quit working, which leads me to believe it's the switch.  I have never seen a solenoid go bad.....not to say that they don't, just that it's not typical.<P>LMK what you find out......I have several good used switches, relays and solenoids (some new switches too).||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTBro||11-20-2000||03:53 PM||||I accidently found out one day that the switch only works when the latch is making contact with the base.  I was in a hurry packing stuff in the trunk and closed the trunk on some sheets or a blanket or something and then I went to open the trunk with the switch and nothing happened.  This was after I had just bought the car.  When I had bought the car, I found out that the key switch for the trunk didn't work...  So then my deck lid was closed and no way to open it...  But I tried the key again and it worked and has worked ever since...  When I opened the lid I saw the sheet was keeping the lock from contacting the latch at the bottom..||||reg||7
Z||000007||theogre||11-20-2000||07:25 PM||||The 4 wire deck lid will not operate the release if the latch isn't grounding thru the ring. The release only uses one of the 4 wires. The other three are used for the "ajar" circuit and, if equiped, the trunk light. The 5th wire on the drivers side is only to ground the metal RFI shield on the lid and has nothing to do with the latch.<P>there's an article in my cave about this. It has the emergency access methods for bypassing the solinoid and switch.<P>the easiest relay test for most people is to take the horn relay from next to the chime and stuff that into the trunk circuit. It's the same relay just a stronger version.<P>Automatic tranny must be in park to work the relay.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||11-20-2000||10:05 PM||||To add to Ogre's stuff -if it's a manual and the engine is running the E- brake must be engaged||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dan87GT||11-21-2000||10:29 AM||||I got it working last night, I jumpered the two small wires on the relay. I have my interor out and was installing a keyless door lock/trunk lid entry I guess something is disconnected in the safety circuit.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||11-21-2000||07:21 PM||||my electric release was totally screwed up when i bought the car. I used the stock switch, and the solenoid was in the car with no wires attached. I just ran 2 new wires from the solenoid to the switch. works great key on or off, but do have to remember not to hit it driving down the road or I engage my air brakes.||||reg||1
